# Public enum variants whose payload is a mutable container. Reading the
# variant hands the container to the caller exactly as a public field
# would, so the default rule is "make the payload own its data". These are
# the chart mirror's explicit AST nodes: the builder functions copy their
# input, and a caller that writes the variant directly is the owner of the
# array it passes (the mirror's documented construction contract). Each
# line is the variant's `Enum::Variant` key and the reason it stays.
#
VegaBins::Values — chart mirror: `values` builder copies; direct AST construction owns its array
VegaChannelSort::Values — chart mirror: `values` builder copies; direct AST construction owns its array
VegaDomain::Values — chart mirror: `values` builder copies; direct AST construction owns its array
VegaPredicate::And — chart mirror: `all_of` copies; direct AST construction owns its array
VegaPredicate::OneOf — chart mirror: `one_of` copies; direct AST construction owns its array
VegaPredicate::Or — chart mirror: `any_of` copies; direct AST construction owns its array
VegaRange::Values — chart mirror: `values` builder copies; direct AST construction owns its array
